WEBVTT

00:00.607 --> 00:03.476
<i>♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪</i>

00:03.889 --> 00:07.158
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.193 --> 00:10.729
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.763 --> 00:13.732
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.766 --> 00:17.235
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.269 --> 00:20.538
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.573 --> 00:22.107
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.141 --> 00:23.475
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.509 --> 00:25.016
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.019 --> 00:35.653
We now return

00:35.688 --> 00:38.656
<i>to The Autistic Postman Always
Rings Four Hundred Times.</i>

00:44.296 --> 00:47.265
So is everybody excited
for Father's Day on Sunday?

00:47.299 --> 00:48.600
Oh, yeah,
that's right.

00:48.634 --> 00:50.935
I always try to avoid
Father's Day now.

00:50.970 --> 00:52.937
Every year, I used to take
my dad to the horse track.

00:52.972 --> 00:56.007
Now we just go rooting around
for bargains at the mall.

00:56.041 --> 00:58.676
Oh, this is darling, isn't it?
Uh-huh.

00:58.711 --> 01:01.159
Glenn, do you think you'd see
my bra through this blouse?

01:01.183 --> 01:01.713
Uh, I don't know.

01:01.714 --> 01:03.681
Is it too sheer?
I don't know what that means.

01:03.716 --> 01:05.016
Glenn? Do you think
it's too sheer?

01:05.050 --> 01:06.651
I said I don't know!

01:06.685 --> 01:08.319
Hey, Joe, you know,
come to think of it,

01:08.354 --> 01:09.320
I've met
Cleveland's dad,

01:09.355 --> 01:10.989
and my dog slept
with Quagmire's dad,

01:11.023 --> 01:12.657
but I don't know anything
about your dad.

01:12.691 --> 01:13.992
Yeah, is he
still with us,

01:14.026 --> 01:16.661
or is he living in Heaven
with Jesus Christ?

01:16.695 --> 01:18.663
Ugh, save that
for your black friends.

01:18.697 --> 01:20.331
Eh, my dad's out
there somewhere,

01:20.366 --> 01:22.000
but I haven't spoken
to him in years.

01:22.034 --> 01:23.301
What?! Really?!

01:23.335 --> 01:24.969
Sorry, Cleveland,
that was mean of me.

01:25.004 --> 01:26.838
I already forgave you.

01:26.872 --> 01:28.873
But, Joe, why haven't you
seen your dad?

01:28.908 --> 01:31.209
Well, he's a good guy,
but we just drifted apart.

01:31.243 --> 01:32.377
It's no big deal.

01:32.411 --> 01:33.945
It's a very big deal.

01:33.979 --> 01:35.819
My dad's a stinking drunk
who lives in Ireland,

01:35.848 --> 01:37.382
but you got
a perfectly good dad.

01:37.416 --> 01:38.716
You can't waste that.

01:38.751 --> 01:40.451
You gotta call him up
for Father's Day.

01:40.486 --> 01:42.787
Peter, I don't even know
where he is.

01:42.822 --> 01:45.023
Who's ready for another beer?

01:45.057 --> 01:47.358
Hey, Cleveland, weren't you
supposed to buy the next round?

01:47.393 --> 01:49.694
That's a shame Joe
never sees his dad.

01:49.728 --> 01:50.695
I know.

01:50.729 --> 01:51.696
Hey, you know what?

01:51.730 --> 01:53.031
Joe's our friend.

01:53.033 --> 01:54.673
He should be with his dad
on Father's Day,

01:54.700 --> 01:56.000
and we're gonna
track him down.

01:56.035 --> 01:58.002
Yeah, that's a
good idea, Peter.

01:58.037 --> 01:59.671
Well, I like
helping people out.

01:59.705 --> 02:02.273
That's why I was such a good
break-up rodeo clown.

02:02.308 --> 02:04.275
I'm just gonna go
ahead and tell you.

02:04.310 --> 02:05.610
I've been sleeping
with your sister.

02:05.644 --> 02:06.945
What?!

02:06.979 --> 02:08.379
Hey, now! Hey, now!
Over here! Over here!

02:08.414 --> 02:10.148
Over here! Hey, now!
Hey, now! Over here!

02:10.182 --> 02:11.482
Over here!
Hey, now! Hey, now!

02:11.517 --> 02:12.483
Over here! Over here!

02:15.855 --> 02:17.488
Oh, and now that
I'm inside the barrel,

02:17.523 --> 02:20.024
he gave you
and your sister HPV.

02:23.495 --> 02:25.463
Hey, want to see
something?

02:25.497 --> 02:27.465
Check out how hot
my last patient was.

02:27.499 --> 02:28.466
Oh.

02:28.500 --> 02:29.467
They look fake.

02:29.501 --> 02:30.501
Yeah, who cares?

02:30.536 --> 02:32.837
Okay, according
to this projection,

02:32.872 --> 02:35.240
Stewie's adult height
will be five-foot-one.

02:35.274 --> 02:36.241
What?!

02:36.275 --> 02:37.976
Five-foot-one?!

02:38.010 --> 02:40.645
Wow, Dr. Hartman,
that's really short.

02:40.679 --> 02:43.982
I mean, I suppose it's fine
if he's gonna die at 14.

02:44.016 --> 02:45.984
Is-is there anything
on there about that?

02:46.018 --> 02:47.652
Well, we learned
in medical school

02:47.686 --> 02:49.320
that the short ones
do go faster,

02:49.355 --> 02:51.356
'cause they smell more farts
than the rest of us.

02:51.390 --> 02:52.357
This is terrible!

02:52.391 --> 02:53.858
I can't be short!

02:53.893 --> 02:57.262
I'll be an outcast, like Rudolph
the Uncircumcised Reindeer.

02:57.296 --> 02:59.264
Look, Rudolph, it's
not me, all right?

02:59.298 --> 03:01.266
It's Dasher, he's
been complaining,

03:01.300 --> 03:03.268
and he is the one who has
to look at it all night.

03:03.302 --> 03:04.602
I don't know.

03:04.637 --> 03:06.938
Mrs. Claus says
it'll decrease my sensitivity.

03:06.972 --> 03:09.908
I-I'm sorry, why are you
talking to my wife about this?

03:13.879 --> 03:15.847
Okay, you guys,
it's all set.

03:15.881 --> 03:17.515
I found Joe's dad
on the Internet,

03:17.549 --> 03:19.851
and he just e-mailed me
to say he's coming tomorrow.

03:19.885 --> 03:22.186
All right, great, but remember,
this is a surprise for Joe.

03:22.221 --> 03:23.521
Why are you
looking at me?

03:23.555 --> 03:24.856
Because you're terrible
at keeping secrets.

03:24.890 --> 03:26.524
No, I'm not;
I'm great at it.

03:26.558 --> 03:28.593
Like when I was
an OB/GYN.

03:28.627 --> 03:30.261
Well, I got the results
of your ultrasound,

03:30.296 --> 03:31.596
and I got some
news for you.

03:31.630 --> 03:32.931
Wait, wait, wait--

03:32.965 --> 03:34.565
We don't want to know
if it's a boy or a girl.

03:34.600 --> 03:35.900
Oh, okay.

03:35.935 --> 03:38.269
<i>Well, it's
not breathing.</i>

03:38.304 --> 03:39.270
Hey, guys.

03:39.305 --> 03:41.940
Uh, uh, so, Joe,
big day tomorrow, eh?

03:41.974 --> 03:43.241
Father's Day.

03:43.275 --> 03:45.910
Gonna be home all day,
especially at 11:30 a.m.?

03:45.945 --> 03:46.759
Peter.

03:46.783 --> 03:47.912
What? I didn't say
anything about his dad.

03:47.913 --> 03:48.880
My dad?

03:48.914 --> 03:50.548
What about my dad?

03:50.582 --> 03:54.619
Well, now that Quagmire ruined
the surprise, we found your dad!

03:54.653 --> 03:55.653
You what?!

03:55.688 --> 03:56.821
That's right.

03:56.855 --> 03:58.189
He's coming tomorrow,
for Father's Day.

03:58.223 --> 04:00.191
You shouldn't have
done that, Peter.

04:00.225 --> 04:02.193
My father's not gonna
be happy to see me.

04:02.227 --> 04:03.528
Sure he will.

04:03.562 --> 04:05.196
Just get him one of them
Father's Day cards

04:05.230 --> 04:06.531
what plays a song.

04:06.565 --> 04:07.532
"Dad to the Bone."

04:07.566 --> 04:09.033
"I'm Dad."

04:09.068 --> 04:11.703
Pretty much anything with
"bad," you turn it to "dad."

04:11.737 --> 04:13.705
Wait, w-why wouldn't
your dad be happy?

04:13.739 --> 04:15.239
What, is he a jerk
or something?

04:15.274 --> 04:18.242
No, it's just that
ever since I was a little kid,

04:18.277 --> 04:21.479
he was constantly making
fun of handicapped people.

04:21.513 --> 04:23.815
Really?
Yeah, my whole life,

04:23.849 --> 04:27.151
my-my dad would ridicule
anyone in a wheelchair.

04:27.186 --> 04:29.487
It was all,
"Hey, spaghetti legs!"

04:29.521 --> 04:31.823
And, "Hey, rigatoni legs!"

04:31.857 --> 04:34.492
And, uh, "Hey,
angel-hair legs!"

04:34.526 --> 04:37.528
He was a sales manager
at Ronzoni.

04:37.563 --> 04:39.864
Wow, then it must have been
hard for him to accept

04:39.898 --> 04:41.199
when you were
paralyzed.

04:41.233 --> 04:42.533
That's just it.

04:42.568 --> 04:44.869
My dad doesn't know
I'm handicapped.

04:44.903 --> 04:46.237
I never told him.

04:46.271 --> 04:49.574
I never...
I never told him!

04:51.377 --> 04:52.677
Ah, Joe, don't cry.

04:52.711 --> 04:54.145
It's gonna make me cry.

04:55.381 --> 04:57.015
I cry like Snoopy.

05:03.357 --> 05:06.559
I can't believe you invited
my father without telling me.

05:06.593 --> 05:08.427
You guys got to get
in touch with him

05:08.462 --> 05:09.662
and tell him
not to come.

05:09.696 --> 05:11.330
It's too late, Joe,
he's already on his way.

05:11.365 --> 05:12.331
He is?

05:12.366 --> 05:13.666
Yeah, we got him
tickets on Kayak.

05:13.700 --> 05:15.668
It is a nightmare
itinerary.

05:15.702 --> 05:17.670
It was, like, 80 bucks,
but he has four stops.

05:17.704 --> 05:19.505
Two of them are
in Houston.

05:19.539 --> 05:20.840
What am I gonna do?

05:20.874 --> 05:23.109
My dad has no idea
I'm paralyzed.

05:23.143 --> 05:25.111
Well, there's only
one thing we can do.

05:25.145 --> 05:26.445
We'll just figure out a way

05:26.480 --> 05:28.214
to hide your handicap
from your dad.

05:28.248 --> 05:30.216
Hide the fact
that I can't walk?

05:30.250 --> 05:31.884
Peter, that'll
never work.

05:31.918 --> 05:32.885
It's worth a try.

05:32.919 --> 05:34.553
Come on, Joe,
don't be so negative.

05:34.588 --> 05:36.322
You're like a Boston
fortune cookie.

05:38.025 --> 05:39.325
"I don't know, numbnuts.

05:39.359 --> 05:42.328
Maybe buy a garage and fill it
with hockey equipment."

05:42.362 --> 05:43.663
Huh.

05:43.697 --> 05:45.665
Well, let's see
what my lucky numbers are.

05:45.699 --> 05:48.000
"Screw you, math dick."

05:48.035 --> 05:50.569
Well, that wasn't
very helpful at all.

05:55.575 --> 05:56.776
Here you go, Stewie.

05:56.810 --> 05:58.878
I know clothes shopping
always cheers you up.

05:58.912 --> 06:01.514
I can't believe I'm only
going to be five-foot-one.

06:01.548 --> 06:03.149
Aw, come on, look
at the bright side.

06:03.183 --> 06:05.217
You'll be in the front row
of every class picture.

06:05.252 --> 06:06.519
Holding that little plaque.

06:06.553 --> 06:07.753
You suck.

06:07.788 --> 06:09.622
Why don't you go drink out
of the fountain?

06:09.656 --> 06:10.890
I'll text you
when I'm done.

06:10.924 --> 06:12.491
I know you're
trying to be rude,

06:12.526 --> 06:14.860
but I am gonna do that,
because I find it enjoyable.

06:19.032 --> 06:20.599
Excuse me, I was
looking at this.

06:20.634 --> 06:22.668
Sorry, I've made a decision
to go for that shirt,

06:22.703 --> 06:24.170
and when that happens,
it is on.

06:24.204 --> 06:25.671
Full throttle, man. Pow!

06:25.706 --> 06:27.673
Wow, you're an energetic
little fellow.

06:27.708 --> 06:29.675
I guess your mommy lets
you drink coffee, huh?

06:29.710 --> 06:32.344
Whoa, whoa, I-I don't put
stimulants in my body.

06:32.379 --> 06:33.679
You know something?

06:33.714 --> 06:35.214
You kind of remind me
of Tom Cruise.

06:35.248 --> 06:36.215
Boom.

06:37.584 --> 06:39.251
You-you got me, man.

06:39.286 --> 06:41.587
Wow,
Tom Cruise.

06:41.621 --> 06:44.590
You look, um...
bigger in the movies.

06:44.624 --> 06:45.925
Wh-What are you doing here?

06:45.959 --> 06:48.928
Oh, I get all my clothes from
out-of-the-way toddler stores.

06:48.962 --> 06:50.930
Ooh, uh, you want
an animal cracker?

06:50.964 --> 06:52.598
Sure, you got
a lion in there?

06:52.632 --> 06:54.266
Oh, no,
I eat those first.

06:54.301 --> 06:56.602
I believe eating
the lions gives me power.

06:56.636 --> 06:59.538
Yeah, I hear you believe
in a lot of crazy stuff.

06:59.573 --> 07:01.207
What'd you get there?
A giraffe?

07:01.241 --> 07:02.208
Yeah.

07:02.242 --> 07:03.209
Good, good.

07:03.243 --> 07:04.210
It's good for eyesight.

07:04.244 --> 07:05.544
Well, you're certainly upbeat.

07:05.579 --> 07:07.546
Let me ask you,
doesn't it bother you

07:07.581 --> 07:09.548
being an adult man
who's that short?

07:09.583 --> 07:11.250
'Cause the doctor says
that's where I'm headed.

07:11.284 --> 07:12.251
Oh, no way, man.

07:12.285 --> 07:14.587
The middle of the word
"short" is "or."

07:14.621 --> 07:16.255
"Or" gives you a choice.

07:16.289 --> 07:18.657
And I choose not to be short.

07:18.692 --> 07:21.060
Wow, you need a road map
for that one.

07:21.094 --> 07:22.061
Hey, hey,
I'll tell you what.

07:22.095 --> 07:23.395
You spend the day with me,

07:23.430 --> 07:25.064
you'll see how great
it is to be short.

07:25.098 --> 07:27.399
You'll feel like
you're discovering a new world.

07:27.434 --> 07:29.068
And you know what's in
the middle of the word "world"?

07:29.102 --> 07:30.736
Um... "or"?

07:30.771 --> 07:32.071
Yes!

07:32.105 --> 07:34.073
The dots have appeared, man,
let's connect them!

07:35.442 --> 07:37.977
You're... you're a weirdo,
but let's do this.

07:41.782 --> 07:43.082
All right, check
it out, Bonnie.

07:43.116 --> 07:45.084
This is how we're
gonna fool Joe's dad.

07:45.118 --> 07:46.752
Oh, my God.

07:46.787 --> 07:48.154
Yeah, looks
real, right?

07:48.188 --> 07:50.489
I put this pair of pants
on the front legs of this horse

07:50.524 --> 07:51.824
and strapped Joe
to the front

07:51.858 --> 07:53.826
with his legs tied
behind the horse's neck.

07:53.860 --> 07:56.495
And then we put Cinnamon's head
up the back of Joe's shirt

07:56.530 --> 07:58.770
and simply hid the rest of the
horse behind this curtain.

08:00.133 --> 08:02.034
His breath is very
moist, Peter.

08:02.068 --> 08:05.037
And to induce movement, I'm
gonna snap the horse's balls

08:05.071 --> 08:06.405
with this dampened
kitchen towel.

08:07.741 --> 08:08.707
Aah! Oh, my God!

08:08.742 --> 08:10.042
Holy crap, he's
out of control!

08:10.076 --> 08:11.944
Does it look real?

08:14.147 --> 08:15.147
Plan B! an B!

08:26.193 --> 08:29.495
Peter, I'm
raid this is hopeless.

08:29.529 --> 08:30.830
What, I don't know
what else to do.

08:30.864 --> 08:32.164
I mean, we're not
gonna come up

08:32.199 --> 08:33.833
with something better
than the horse.

08:33.867 --> 08:35.835
Yeah, I guess you're just
gonna have to tell your dad

08:35.869 --> 08:37.169
about your handicap.

08:37.204 --> 08:38.838
I can't do that.

08:38.872 --> 08:41.774
If you guys were in my shoes,
you'd understand.

08:41.808 --> 08:43.776
Wait a minute, that's it!

08:43.810 --> 08:45.778
<i>I will get in your shoes.</i>

08:45.812 --> 08:47.413
I'll just pretend to be you.

08:47.447 --> 08:49.081
I mean, your dad ain't
seen you in years.

08:49.115 --> 08:50.416
He won't know
the difference.

08:50.450 --> 08:51.951
What? That's crazy.

08:53.320 --> 08:55.287
Boy, that was a close call.

08:55.322 --> 08:58.023
Is some of this room cold?

09:01.995 --> 09:03.329
All right, Peter,
almost done.

09:05.665 --> 09:07.299
Huh? Huh?

09:07.334 --> 09:08.300
Eh, kind of.

09:08.335 --> 09:10.035
Yeah.
I don't care.

09:10.070 --> 09:11.704
Peter, I don't
know about this.

09:11.738 --> 09:13.038
It seems like
a bad idea.

09:13.073 --> 09:15.708
Look, Lois, Joe is one
of my best friends, all right?

09:15.742 --> 09:17.376
I'm only doing this
to help him.

09:17.410 --> 09:19.044
Besides, wait till you hear
my "Joe" voice.

09:19.079 --> 09:22.047
Uh, God, I hate
being stuck in this chair.

09:22.082 --> 09:24.884
No, Peter,
that fights it.

09:24.918 --> 09:27.553
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

09:27.587 --> 09:30.556
♪ Mr. Big Stuff ♪

09:30.590 --> 09:32.558
♪ Who do you think you are? ♪

09:32.592 --> 09:34.627
♪ Mr. Big Stuff ♪

09:34.661 --> 09:37.529
♪ You're never gonna
get my love ♪

09:37.564 --> 09:39.999
♪ Now because you wear ♪

09:40.033 --> 09:42.635
♪ All those fancy clothes ♪

09:42.669 --> 09:43.869
<i>♪ Oh, yeah ♪</i>

09:43.904 --> 09:46.572
♪ And have a big fine car ♪

09:46.606 --> 09:48.507
♪ Oh, yes, you do now ♪

09:48.541 --> 09:50.242
♪ Do you think I can afford ♪

09:50.277 --> 09:52.244
♪ To give you my love ♪

09:52.279 --> 09:53.746
<i>♪ Oh, yeah ♪</i>

09:53.780 --> 09:57.583
♪ You think you're higher
than every star above ♪

09:57.617 --> 09:59.685
♪ Mr. Big Stuff ♪

10:01.254 --> 10:03.055
♪ Who do you think you are? ♪

10:03.089 --> 10:05.090
♪ Mr. Big Stuff ♪

10:06.426 --> 10:08.394
♪ You're never gonna
make me cry ♪

10:08.428 --> 10:09.895
♪ Mr. Big Stuff ♪

10:09.930 --> 10:11.230
♪ Tell me, tell me... ♪

10:13.934 --> 10:15.234
That's Bud.

10:15.268 --> 10:16.235
Are you ready, Peter?

10:16.269 --> 10:17.236
I think so.

10:17.270 --> 10:18.570
What do you think,
acting coach?

10:18.605 --> 10:22.241
I think you will be
exemplary, Peter.

10:22.275 --> 10:24.576
All good acting coaches
are insane old ladies.

10:24.611 --> 10:26.178
Emote!

10:28.214 --> 10:29.181
Hi, Bud.

10:29.215 --> 10:30.182
Hi, Joe's dad.

10:30.216 --> 10:31.517
Uh, I mean, uh, Dad.

10:31.551 --> 10:33.085
Uh, Joe, I'm Joe;
you're my dad.

10:33.119 --> 10:34.153
Joe?

10:34.187 --> 10:36.288
Wow, I guess it really
has been a long time.

10:36.323 --> 10:37.690
I barely recognize you.

10:37.724 --> 10:39.191
Put on a little weight,
haven't you?

10:39.225 --> 10:41.226
Well, I could say
the same for you.

10:42.963 --> 10:45.898
Sometimes I don't
understand why people laugh.

10:49.636 --> 10:51.503
All right, everyone in the car.

10:51.538 --> 10:53.472
We got a Father's Day
dinner reservation.

10:53.506 --> 10:55.541
Why is Mr. Swanson coming?

10:55.575 --> 10:57.109
And why is he dressed like Dad?

10:57.143 --> 10:58.377
I don't know, kids.

10:58.411 --> 11:01.380
I stopped asking after your
father said he shot a horse.

11:05.919 --> 11:07.786
Thanks for
the ride-along.

11:07.821 --> 11:10.322
I liked when you sentenced those
two girls to kiss each other.

11:10.357 --> 11:12.925
Yeah, all girls are lesbians
when you point a gun at 'em.

11:12.959 --> 11:15.194
Boy, it's been great
spending time with you, son.

11:15.228 --> 11:17.896
It's been great spending
time with you, too...

11:17.931 --> 11:19.098
Dad.

11:21.668 --> 11:23.102
Oh, this'll be fun.

11:23.136 --> 11:24.436
Let's see how long it takes them

11:24.471 --> 11:26.171
to get Gumby over there
into the car.

11:26.206 --> 11:28.107
Yeah, that's our neighbor,
Peter Griffin.

11:28.141 --> 11:29.608
That's the guy
who e-mailed me?

11:29.642 --> 11:32.678
Huh, no wonder it was all caps
with tons of typos.

11:32.712 --> 11:33.946
He's a water head, right?

11:33.980 --> 11:35.180
Yeah, he's a mess.

11:35.215 --> 11:36.382
Look at his ugly kids.

11:36.416 --> 11:38.317
Pathetic.

11:38.351 --> 11:39.852
Ugh, he's not fitting.

11:39.886 --> 11:42.955
Just put some of him
in the back like skis.

11:47.460 --> 11:48.627
Hey, Stewie.
What's up?

11:48.661 --> 11:50.162
When you
say it like that,

11:50.196 --> 11:51.430
you sound just
like Tom Cruise.

11:51.464 --> 11:52.765
What?
Oh, yeah,

11:52.799 --> 11:54.033
I've been hanging
with Tom Cruise.

11:54.067 --> 11:55.868
You've been hanging out
with Tom Cruise?

11:55.902 --> 11:56.869
Sure have.

11:56.903 --> 11:58.170
We spent the whole
day together,

11:58.204 --> 11:59.338
and he showed me

11:59.372 --> 12:00.773
there's a lot of
advantages to being short.

12:00.807 --> 12:01.940
Oh, yeah? Like what?

12:01.975 --> 12:03.542
You're the last one
to get wet when it rains?

12:03.576 --> 12:04.777
Well, yeah, that.

12:04.811 --> 12:06.912
And you can chow
pie standing up.

12:06.946 --> 12:08.781
We didn't do any of that,
but the point is,

12:08.815 --> 12:10.449
I'm at peace
with being short.

12:10.483 --> 12:11.950
Full throttle, man!
Pow!

12:13.520 --> 12:14.787
Hello?

12:14.821 --> 12:16.722
Oh, hi,
Dr. Hartman.

12:16.756 --> 12:18.590
Mrs. Griffin,
I have some good news.

12:18.625 --> 12:20.959
Turns out your son
is going to be normal height.

12:20.994 --> 12:23.028
I read his chart wrong
yesterday.

12:23.063 --> 12:26.231
Apparently, I have something
called "dislooxia"?

12:26.266 --> 12:28.067
That was the doctor.

12:28.101 --> 12:30.969
Apparently, Stewie's not
gonna be short after all.

12:31.004 --> 12:32.538
What? Really?

12:32.572 --> 12:33.906
That's wonderful news!

12:33.940 --> 12:35.374
Oh, I'm so relieved

12:35.408 --> 12:37.509
my child is spared
some heartache.

12:37.544 --> 12:39.978
Now, come on, Brian, I guess
we should try to make it

12:40.013 --> 12:41.146
over to Meg's
birthday party.

12:44.017 --> 12:46.085
Could I have some bread
while I open my presents?

12:46.119 --> 12:47.786
At this point,
we're gonna have to start

12:47.821 --> 12:49.321
charging you
for the bread.

12:51.257 --> 12:52.224
Hey, Stewie!

12:52.258 --> 12:53.425
You want to check out
the go-kart

12:53.460 --> 12:54.660
<i>I used in Days of Thunder?</i>

12:54.694 --> 12:55.928
Yeah, listen, um...

12:55.962 --> 12:58.363
I just found out I'm
actually going to be tall,

12:58.398 --> 13:01.200
so I'm no longer comfortable
hanging out with someone

13:01.234 --> 13:03.001
whose teeth are bigger
than their fingers.

13:03.036 --> 13:04.036
What?

13:04.070 --> 13:05.370
That's...
that's barely true.

13:05.405 --> 13:07.005
Yeah, so...
see you later.

13:07.040 --> 13:08.841
You are making a big mistake,
Stewie!

13:08.875 --> 13:12.211
Nobody walks away
from Tiny Tom Cruise!

13:12.245 --> 13:13.879
Yeah, except for
all three of your wives.

13:13.913 --> 13:15.681
Okay, I'm
shutting this now.

13:15.715 --> 13:18.784
Okay, so... bye!

13:22.355 --> 13:25.958
So now, since I switched
to disposable catheters,

13:25.992 --> 13:29.294
I no longer have those beet-red
infections in my urethra.

13:29.329 --> 13:30.329
Oh, no.

13:30.363 --> 13:31.563
I hope it's not genetic.

13:31.598 --> 13:33.165
Chris, he's
not our dad.

13:33.199 --> 13:35.234
I can't keep up with this ruse.

13:35.268 --> 13:36.702
Hey, everybody!

13:36.736 --> 13:38.470
Peter, finally,
you're home.

13:38.505 --> 13:40.405
How's it going over there
with my dad?

13:40.440 --> 13:42.241
Awesome. He fell for
the whole thing.

13:42.275 --> 13:44.042
In fact, we've been
having a great time!

13:44.077 --> 13:45.711
Wow, that's
terrific, Peter!

13:45.745 --> 13:48.180
You'll only have to pull it
off for a few more hours.

13:48.214 --> 13:50.883
Then he'll be on a plane
tomorrow and I can go home.

13:50.917 --> 13:52.217
Oh, that's
the other good news.

13:52.252 --> 13:53.619
Bud's not leaving!

13:53.653 --> 13:55.287
I told him he can move in
with me and Bonnie.

13:55.321 --> 13:56.288
What?!

13:56.322 --> 13:57.589
Peter, this is crazy!

13:57.624 --> 13:59.224
Na it's gonna
work out fine.

13:59.259 --> 14:00.392
Oh, and remember, Joe,

14:00.426 --> 14:01.894
if Lois is feeling
frisky at night,

14:01.928 --> 14:04.363
it's index finger
around and clockwise.

14:04.397 --> 14:05.864
And just keep
doing that to yourself

14:05.899 --> 14:07.132
until you're good to go.

14:11.692 --> 14:13.660
<i>Peter, this is ridiculous.</i>

14:13.694 --> 14:16.796
You can't live in my house
with my dad and my family!

14:16.830 --> 14:19.165
Your dad got me
super clean in the tub.

14:19.199 --> 14:20.967
Joe's right,
this is idiotic.

14:21.001 --> 14:22.268
What are you thinking?

14:22.302 --> 14:23.536
I'll tell you what I'm thinking.

14:23.570 --> 14:25.204
I'm thinking that
I've had two dads

14:25.239 --> 14:27.674
and neither one cared for me
as much as Bud does.

14:27.708 --> 14:29.042
Peter, I've had
enough of this!

14:29.076 --> 14:30.610
You can't just
take my dad!

14:30.644 --> 14:31.811
Well, he's right
next door.

14:31.845 --> 14:33.613
Nothing's stopping you
from going over there

14:33.647 --> 14:34.947
and telling him the truth:

14:34.982 --> 14:37.483
that his son is a paraplegic
who's stuck in a wheelchair.

14:37.518 --> 14:38.885
You know I
can't do that.

14:38.919 --> 14:40.620
Ah, suit yourself.
But I gotta go.

14:40.654 --> 14:42.422
Me and Bud are
having a blast.

14:44.124 --> 14:45.525
I'm sorry, Joe.

14:45.559 --> 14:46.859
A-Are you okay?

14:46.894 --> 14:48.227
Not really.

14:48.262 --> 14:49.996
I'll be honest,
Lois, this hurts.

14:50.030 --> 14:51.764
Hurts like the Dickens.

14:51.799 --> 14:53.733
I've finished
my latest novel.

14:53.767 --> 14:54.767
Splendid, Charles!

14:54.802 --> 14:55.768
What is it called?

14:55.803 --> 14:56.969
<i>Oliver Nipple-Twist.</i>

14:57.004 --> 14:58.037
Ow!

14:58.072 --> 14:59.639
Oh, Charles, you bastard!

14:59.673 --> 15:00.873
Yeah! The Dickens!

15:00.908 --> 15:03.042
It hurts like the me!

15:08.582 --> 15:12.018
So, anyone going to
the gerbil's funeral on Friday?

15:12.052 --> 15:13.152
Okay, kids!

15:13.187 --> 15:15.054
Everyone in a circle
for parachute time.

15:15.089 --> 15:18.024
Oh, goodie,
I love parachute time!

15:20.527 --> 15:22.729
Whee!

15:22.763 --> 15:24.464
Whee!

15:25.299 --> 15:26.933
Whee!

15:26.967 --> 15:28.601
What the hell?

15:28.635 --> 15:30.870
That kid looked like
Tiny Tom Cruise.

15:30.904 --> 15:32.171
Whee!

15:32.206 --> 15:34.307
Huh.
Must've been my imagination.

15:35.476 --> 15:36.476
Aah!

15:36.510 --> 15:38.444
If you think
you're getting away from me,

15:38.479 --> 15:40.179
you've got a crazy laugh
coming, friend.

15:42.616 --> 15:44.083
Aah!

15:52.793 --> 15:54.127
Hey, what are you doing home
so early?

15:54.161 --> 15:55.128
He's following me, Brian!

15:55.162 --> 15:56.195
Who's following you?

15:56.230 --> 15:57.396
Tom Cruise!

15:57.431 --> 15:59.065
I spend one afternoon
with the guy,

15:59.099 --> 16:00.733
and it's like I signed
an eight-year contract

16:00.768 --> 16:02.201
to show up at events with him

16:02.236 --> 16:03.936
and let him fake-father a child.

16:03.971 --> 16:05.638
Stewie, I would think Tom Cruise

16:05.672 --> 16:07.740
has better things to do
than follow you around.

16:07.775 --> 16:08.741
Oh, really?

16:08.776 --> 16:09.842
Well, explain that!

16:17.217 --> 16:19.452
You know, it's times
like this where I think,

16:19.486 --> 16:21.687
if I didn't talk and
you were a normal baby,

16:21.722 --> 16:23.422
we wouldn't have
any of these problems.

16:23.457 --> 16:24.757
You gotta help me
get rid of him, Brian!

16:24.792 --> 16:26.425
He's creepier
than that guy at the gym

16:26.460 --> 16:28.427
who just does karate
in the mirror.

16:30.197 --> 16:31.297
It's me.

16:31.331 --> 16:32.298
The guy's me.

16:32.332 --> 16:33.733
I'm a gym karate creep.

16:36.937 --> 16:38.037
I'm pretty good, too.

16:38.071 --> 16:39.205
But relax.

16:39.239 --> 16:41.240
If I wanted you dead,
you'd be dead.

16:45.012 --> 16:47.280
Hey, Dad, what do you
say we go play catch?

16:47.314 --> 16:48.447
And throw me
some divers.

16:48.482 --> 16:50.983
I want to get grass stains
on my school slacks.

16:51.018 --> 16:52.018
What?

16:52.052 --> 16:53.186
You're a grown man.

16:53.220 --> 16:55.354
I know, it's just so
great having a dad.

16:55.389 --> 16:57.857
Well, it's nice having
reconnected with you, too.

16:57.891 --> 17:00.426
All right, let's do it.

17:06.867 --> 17:08.167
Oh, for God's sake.

17:08.202 --> 17:10.169
See, a guy like that
should just stay inside

17:10.204 --> 17:11.504
so we don't have
to look at him.

17:11.538 --> 17:12.738
Joe, go over there

17:12.773 --> 17:14.207
and tell him to get
back in his house.

17:14.241 --> 17:16.676
Don't worry, I'll
take care of it.

17:16.710 --> 17:17.910
Joe, you gotta go inside.

17:17.945 --> 17:19.111
You're upsetting my dad.

17:19.146 --> 17:21.013
<i>Your dad?
That's right!</i>

17:21.048 --> 17:22.415
He loves me
in a way that...

17:22.449 --> 17:24.083
Aw, you guys had pizza?

17:24.117 --> 17:25.585
Screw you, Peter!

17:25.619 --> 17:27.186
You know what? This is over!

17:27.221 --> 17:28.387
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

17:28.422 --> 17:29.388
Not a chance.

17:29.423 --> 17:30.723
I like your house better.

17:30.757 --> 17:32.625
I got nothing to hold onto
when I poop at home.

17:32.659 --> 17:35.194
You have no idea how many shower
curtains I've ripped down.

17:35.229 --> 17:36.195
Now get inside.

17:36.230 --> 17:37.930
No, I'm not
gonna do that.

17:37.965 --> 17:39.131
Oh, yes, you are!

17:39.166 --> 17:41.667
Get away from me,
you son of a bitch!

17:41.702 --> 17:43.502
What the hell?

17:43.537 --> 17:45.238
Joe, don't take that
from him!

17:48.275 --> 17:49.542
How do you like that?

17:49.576 --> 17:51.811
You're getting
your ass kicked by a cripple!

17:51.845 --> 17:54.547
A helpless,
spaghetti-legged cripple!

17:54.581 --> 17:55.648
What are you doing?

17:55.682 --> 17:56.782
You're my son!

17:56.817 --> 17:58.117
You can't let yourself
get beat up

17:58.151 --> 17:59.652
by a guy
in a wheelchair!

17:59.686 --> 18:02.889
Your son is a guy
in a wheelchair.

18:02.923 --> 18:04.657
What are you talking about?

18:11.765 --> 18:12.798
Yes.

18:12.833 --> 18:13.933
Yes, Dad.

18:13.967 --> 18:15.268
It's me.

18:17.004 --> 18:18.304
Joe!

18:18.338 --> 18:19.605
What the hell
happened to you?

18:19.640 --> 18:21.274
I was shot in
the line of duty.

18:21.308 --> 18:23.609
"Line of duty."

18:23.644 --> 18:26.779
So, this is why you haven't
called me in all these years?

18:26.813 --> 18:28.114
How could I, Dad?

18:28.148 --> 18:30.049
You always made fun
of handicapped people.

18:30.083 --> 18:33.552
The only thing I never
understood was... why?

18:33.587 --> 18:35.087
I don't know.

18:35.122 --> 18:36.756
I guess I could
never stand the thought

18:36.790 --> 18:38.257
of something like that
happening to me.

18:38.292 --> 18:41.093
Or even worse, to someone
that I care about.

18:41.128 --> 18:43.229
One time, my legs fell
asleep on the toilet.

18:43.263 --> 18:44.897
I had to crawl
into the living room

18:44.932 --> 18:46.332
and interrupt
Lois's book club.

18:46.366 --> 18:48.734
That was one of the shower
curtains I ripped down.

18:48.769 --> 18:51.170
And I suppose, deep down,
I was afraid.

18:51.204 --> 18:52.772
Afraid that, if it did happen,

18:52.806 --> 18:54.607
I wouldn't be strong enough
to handle it.

18:54.641 --> 18:57.310
Well, Dad, I can tell you
from experience

18:57.344 --> 18:59.779
it's only when
your worst fears come true

18:59.813 --> 19:03.049
that you get to find out
how strong you really are.

19:03.083 --> 19:05.618
Then I guess I've got
some learning to do.

19:05.652 --> 19:07.253
I love you, son.

19:07.287 --> 19:08.967
I love you, too, Dad.
I love you, too, Dad.

19:13.727 --> 19:15.194
Hey, Joe, uh,
just one question:

19:15.228 --> 19:17.430
<i>why do you have all those
Wizard of Oz plates?</i>

19:17.464 --> 19:19.298
Because if I finish
my vegetables,

19:19.333 --> 19:21.767
I get to see
the Yellow Brick Road.

19:21.802 --> 19:23.803
All right,
you sold me.

19:27.140 --> 19:28.274
All right, Brian,

19:28.308 --> 19:30.176
Tiny Tom Cruise
is somewhere close.

19:30.210 --> 19:31.777
I can sense
his manic energy.

19:31.812 --> 19:33.112
You remember the plan?

19:33.146 --> 19:34.714
Yup, I got it.

19:34.748 --> 19:37.583
Help, help!
My dog got off his leash!

19:37.617 --> 19:40.186
Is there anyone
who can do a pumpy-arm run?

19:41.655 --> 19:44.490
Running, running, running,
running, running, running, run!

19:44.524 --> 19:47.159
Hey, Stewie. I'm here to help
you for the next billion years.

19:47.194 --> 19:48.427
All right, good to know.

19:48.462 --> 19:50.096
Anyway, my dog ran
around those bushes.

19:50.130 --> 19:51.130
I am on it!

19:52.399 --> 19:54.367
Gotcha!

19:54.401 --> 19:56.268
All right,
off to Zappos with him.

19:56.303 --> 19:57.603
You sure this
is gonna work?

19:57.637 --> 19:59.238
Oh, yeah.
They'll accept any returns.

19:59.272 --> 20:01.173
We don't even
have to pay postage.

20:03.110 --> 20:05.144
Hello, friend.
Your life...

20:05.178 --> 20:06.712
is about to change.

20:06.747 --> 20:09.648
Hey, Tom. It's been
a couple weeks.

20:13.987 --> 20:17.156
Hey, listen, Joe, I'm sorry
I treated you like such a jerk.

20:17.190 --> 20:18.691
Well, that's okay, Peter.

20:18.725 --> 20:21.494
In fact, I got to say, it
was a nice thing you did.

20:21.528 --> 20:24.930
I'm glad I reconnected with
my dad after all these years.

20:24.965 --> 20:26.532
Ah, it was my pleasure.

20:26.566 --> 20:28.467
There's no more important
relationship than...

20:28.502 --> 20:29.802
I'm sorry, Cleveland,
what the hell

20:29.836 --> 20:31.504
is that
Toronto Raptors hat?

20:31.538 --> 20:32.838
It was my
Father's Day present.

20:32.873 --> 20:34.040
I hate it.

20:34.074 --> 20:35.741
I'm just gonna
wear it for a week

20:35.776 --> 20:37.076
then say
I lost it.

20:37.110 --> 20:38.878
Anyway, thanks for
helping me, Peter.

20:38.912 --> 20:40.846
Yeah, it all
worked out great, Joe.

20:40.881 --> 20:43.682
Except I am still missing
that one pair of pants.

20:51.134 --> 20:54.809
Excuse me,
are those Bugle Boy jeans?

20:54.810 --> 20:57.810
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru